WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.067
-Welcome back. We are
hanging out with my co-host

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:04.834
Jack Harlow right here,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:07.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah!

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:09.167
He's currently on tour
with his album

00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:13.100
"Come Home the Kids Miss You,"
which is out right now.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.467
Pick it up right now and
check it out on all the Spotify

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:17.133
and all the things
you listen to music on.

00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:19.734
-Yes. Yes, please.
-Thank you --

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:21.167
Thank you for being here, buddy.

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:24.400
You know, I think you were
a musical guest in 2020.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.667
-That's right.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:28.200
-It was your
first TV appearance.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.734
I think I heard "Whats Poppin"
and I Shazamed it,

00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:35.067
and I was like, "This kid.
Who is this guy? Jack Harlow?

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:37.234
He's amazing."
And they called up.

00:00:37.234 --> 00:00:39.734
And someone was like, "I don't
know if he's ready for TV."

00:00:39.734 --> 00:00:41.167
I mean, the song just --

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:43.000
-Well, I hope
you take this the right way.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.868
I feel like you were very early
for late-night television.

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:48.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:50.133
And, I mean --
I feel like a lot of artists,

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:53.334
when their song finally is
in super rotation on the radio,

00:00:53.334 --> 00:00:55.067
then it's like,
"Okay, let's get him up here."

00:00:55.067 --> 00:00:57.834
You were, to me,
a tastemaker in that moment.

00:00:57.834 --> 00:00:59.334
You were super early, so --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:59.334 --> 00:01:01.367
-That's what I'm talking -- See?
Thank you.

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:03.601
-For real.
You were -- You were really --

00:01:03.601 --> 00:01:05.834
You were really early on that,
so thank you for having me.

00:01:05.834 --> 00:01:07.834
-But I love that you came on
because I was like --

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.434
It really was your
first TV appearance,

00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:11.934
and everyone on your team
was a little kind of nervous.

00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:13.467
You weren't.
You were like, "Let's do this."

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:14.801
-Oh, I was. I was nervous.
-You were?

00:01:14.801 --> 00:01:15.868
-Yeah.
-You didn't show it.

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:17.000
You killed it.
-Can't show it.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.400
-Yeah, you can't show it.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.267
And then it's so fun to watch
your career rise and rise.

00:01:21.267 --> 00:01:23.701
And I recently got to
see you at the VMAs.

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:25.567
Congratulations on
winning all of those.

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:27.667
-Thank you.
-All of those Moon people.

00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:30.167
-Thank you.
-"First Class."

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:31.934
That was awesome.
That's got to feel good.

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:33.601
-It feels amazing.
Song of the summer.

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:35.300
-And then --
and then you asked me to...

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:36.801
to be in the opening with you.
-Yeah.

00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:38.434
-To which I was like,
"Absolutely, buddy.

00:01:38.434 --> 00:01:39.734
I'll do anything for you."

00:01:39.734 --> 00:01:42.467
So, "First Class,"
you did in it, like, a --

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:45.000
Like, we were
in an airplane together.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.567
And so -- Yeah, there's me.

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:49.400
-Wow.
-That's me right there.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.067
-I forgot how cool you looked
in this moment.

00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:52.234
You looked --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:53.634
-I looked pretty cool
right there.

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:55.334
Yeah, I was, like,
just chilling out, man.

00:01:55.334 --> 00:01:58.968
Yeah, exactly.
It was me and Lil Nas X there.

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:00.601
I think Avril Lavigne
is on this plane somewhere.

00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:02.434
-Yeah. All the legends.

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:04.167
-Yeah, we had -- we had --
-Nimo.

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:05.701
-Oh, yeah. Who --

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:07.868
-I think Saucy Santana's
back there. Chloe Bailey.

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:09.501
-Saucy Santana was there,
as well.

00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:10.934
-That was a fun moment.

00:02:10.934 --> 00:02:14.400
-But then you came out and
kind of co-hosted the VMAs.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.100
But who is -- who is this guy
you came out with?

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.367
-I'm so glad you asked.
-Who --

00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:22.334
-This -- His -- His appearance
was off script, you know,

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:24.133
because I was already co-hosting

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:26.267
with the legends Nicki Minaj
and LL Cool J.

00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:27.834
-LL Cool J, yeah.
-So they were expecting me

00:02:27.834 --> 00:02:29.667
to go out on my own, do my part.

00:02:29.667 --> 00:02:31.701
And I was -- been sitting
with Druski throughout the show.

00:02:31.701 --> 00:02:33.501
And I was like, "Yo, you want
to just come with me?"

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:36.200
So this is -- this is Druski.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.701
-So you just grabbed him
and go, "Hey."

00:02:38.701 --> 00:02:40.934
Does he even have a microphone?
-It is -- This is one of my --

00:02:40.934 --> 00:02:42.234
This is one
of my truest friends.

00:02:42.234 --> 00:02:43.534
He didn't have a mic,

00:02:43.534 --> 00:02:45.701
but he would just bend over
and talk into mine.

00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:46.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:48.534
But I was telling you
before the show,

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.968
you got to get him up here.
You got to get this --

00:02:50.968 --> 00:02:52.567
This guy right here.
-Druski.

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:54.934
-He -- If you don't know --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:54.934 --> 00:02:57.033
If you don't know,
keep your eye on this guy.

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:58.234
This guy's a genius.

00:02:58.234 --> 00:02:59.801
-Okay, good. Alright. Druski.

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:02.501
Yeah, we're coming for you, bud.
Alright. Alright, yeah.

00:03:02.501 --> 00:03:04.033
I thought it was great.

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:05.567
You came out, you performed,
you were so good.

00:03:05.567 --> 00:03:07.200
And I know you -- you sample

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.300
a little bit of Fergie
in the song "First Class."

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:11.300
-A lot of bit.
-A lot of bit.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.534
A little bit, a lot of bit.
Yeah.

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:16.133
And you brought out Fergie,
and the place went nuts.

00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:17.400
-Crazy.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.701
-And here she is.
You and Fergie.

00:03:19.701 --> 00:03:21.634
Yeah, that's pretty good.

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.601
And I -- I heard a story

00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:25.567
that you once tried
to perform Fergie at school?

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:27.133
Like, in a talent show
or something?

00:03:27.133 --> 00:03:29.467
-There was, yeah, a talent
show when I was in fifth grade.

00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:32.067
I tried to do "Fergalicious."

00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:34.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.567 --> 00:03:37.334
It's a true story. True story.

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:41.334
And, you know, the lyrics
are suggestive, I guess.

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:42.701
To me --
To me, it wasn't anything.

00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:44.601
-Yeah, you didn't get it
when you're in fifth grade.

00:03:44.601 --> 00:03:46.167
-I didn't even
get to finish the audition.

00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:47.801
I was halfway through,
and they cut me off.

00:03:47.801 --> 00:03:50.167
They're like,
"You can't do that."

00:03:50.167 --> 00:03:53.334
So, that's --
that's my rapper origin story.

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:54.901
-Yes. Yeah, exactly. Yeah.

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:57.400
And then, just recently,
by the way,

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.767
you're in the "Time" 100 Next.

00:03:59.767 --> 00:04:02.434
You're on the list, buddy,
right here.

00:04:02.434 --> 00:04:04.200
There's Keke on the cover.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:06.067 --> 00:04:07.367
There he is. Right there.

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:09.567
Jack Harlow right there
on the "Time" 100.

00:04:09.567 --> 00:04:12.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:16.033
And they -- they asked me
to write your intro.

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:17.934
-Yeah. They know
the connection we have.

00:04:17.934 --> 00:04:20.133
-Yeah, yeah. Did you know
I was going to write it?

00:04:20.133 --> 00:04:21.901
-I had no idea. I woke up to it.
And --

00:04:21.901 --> 00:04:23.934
-Yeah, we didn't tell you.
-Once again, thank you.

00:04:23.934 --> 00:04:25.767
It's been cool to climb
the ladder with you.

00:04:25.767 --> 00:04:27.834
You know, different steps away
from the VMA performance

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.701
to, like you said,
the first time I came on here.

00:04:29.701 --> 00:04:31.000
-Now you're doing
Barclays Center tomorrow.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.667
-Crazy.
-I mean, that's...

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:34.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:36.801
How is -- How's the tour going?

00:04:36.801 --> 00:04:38.334
-It's phenomenal.

00:04:38.334 --> 00:04:40.100
It's my first time
with a live band.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.968
-Yeah.
Do -- Do you like touring?

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:43.901
-I actually like it a lot,
especially in the U.S.

00:04:43.901 --> 00:04:46.367
I like the bus life.
I've gotten sick of the airport.

00:04:46.367 --> 00:04:48.968
So, to me, being able to be in
a bus and wake up in a new city,

00:04:48.968 --> 00:04:51.167
like, it's the dream.
-I was telling everyone today,

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:53.701
you pulled up in a tour bus
this morning.

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:56.000
-To 30 Rock.
-Yeah, right to the --

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.467
-We were --
We were coming from Toronto.

00:04:58.467 --> 00:05:01.300
And we left, I think,
at around 5:00 a.m.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:03.667
-Yeah.
-So, we pull off.

00:05:03.667 --> 00:05:06.133
And we thought we were
going to get here at 1:00.

00:05:06.133 --> 00:05:09.467
And then I wake up at 3:00,
and I open my shades,

00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:12.467
and I look out and I'm just
seeing skyscrapers and taxis.

00:05:12.467 --> 00:05:14.534
-Yeah.
-And I realize we're so late

00:05:14.534 --> 00:05:16.400
that we're headed right here.

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:18.334
-You didn't get a chance
to go to the hotel.

00:05:18.334 --> 00:05:20.167
-Yeah,. It's like,
"Let's -- Let's go. I'm ready."

00:05:20.167 --> 00:05:22.868
-Yeah, exactly right.
You came and showed up.

00:05:22.868 --> 00:05:25.868
Is your --

00:05:25.868 --> 00:05:28.701
Is your mom, I know,
super proud of you, right?

00:05:28.701 --> 00:05:30.701
Yeah. And, yeah, she loves
everything you do.

00:05:30.701 --> 00:05:32.033
I heard the -- the story.

00:05:32.033 --> 00:05:33.801
You guys would freestyle
in your car?

00:05:33.801 --> 00:05:36.033
-Yeah. Yeah, when I was --
when I was super young,

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:38.601
I would plug up to the aux
and put on beats from YouTube.

00:05:38.601 --> 00:05:40.434
-But your mom would freestyle,
as well?

00:05:40.434 --> 00:05:42.567
-She would --
And she would freestyle with me.

00:05:42.567 --> 00:05:44.300
And we would go back and forth.
-That's a mom.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.300
That is a supportive mom
for you right there.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:48.334
-Trust -- Trust me, trust me.
-You know what I'm saying, bud?

00:05:48.334 --> 00:05:50.634
What would your mom
freestyle rap about?

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:52.300
-Oh, she was dark, man.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.734
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.734 --> 00:05:58.100
-What? That's so funny.

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:00.801
-No, she would say things
I can't even say on live TV.

00:06:00.801 --> 00:06:02.467
-Yeah, of course.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:02.467 --> 00:06:04.734
And then you actually used to
record music videos.

00:06:04.734 --> 00:06:07.033
And this is something
you brought us.

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:09.167
I appreciate this. This is
one of your earliest raps.

00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:11.467
Take a look at young
Jack Harlow.

00:06:11.467 --> 00:06:13.968
♪ Oh, I've been getting busy
-working on my next track ♪

00:06:13.968 --> 00:06:16.400
♪ So don't get mad
if you try to text Jack ♪

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:19.300
♪ And he doesn't text back,
I mean, I'm sorry ♪

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:21.767
♪ I wish I could make it
to your birthday party ♪

00:06:21.767 --> 00:06:23.467
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.467 --> 00:06:24.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:26.400
-That's a -- That's a good rap.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.367
Don't be mad
if I don't text back.

00:06:28.367 --> 00:06:31.601
-Listen, man.
I'm from the trenches, man.

00:06:31.601 --> 00:06:34.367
You know?
-I'm happy that you're here.

00:06:34.367 --> 00:06:36.234
We're going to interview
Dwyane Wade together.

00:06:36.234 --> 00:06:38.267
But I just want to say congrats
on everything, bud.

00:06:38.267 --> 00:06:39.968
It's always a pleasure
to watch you.

00:06:39.968 --> 00:06:42.133
Keep going up higher
and higher and higher, buddy.

00:06:42.133 --> 00:06:43.934
-GOAT.
-Come on. Jack Harlow.

00:06:43.934 --> 00:06:45.968
-The GOAT.
-Jack Harlow, everybody.

00:06:45.968 --> 00:06:47.667
For more information on the

00:06:47.667 --> 00:06:49.367
"Come Home the Kids Miss You"
tour,

00:06:49.367 --> 00:06:51.734
go to jackharlow.us.

00:06:51.734 --> 00:06:53.634
Jack and I will be right back
with Dwyane Wade.

00:06:53.634 --> 00:06:54.968
Stick around, everybody.

